<resources>
    <!-- Dark pair for the 1x1 unread-count widget: Quiet Ink's
         `surfaceContainer` under its dark `onSurface`, from
         lib/theme/app_theme.dart. A tile one step up from the app's own
         surface, because it sits on a wallpaper rather than in a scaffold.

         It was `_npInk` under the light theme's cream — Newspaper's values on
         a widget that has nothing to do with Newspaper.

         **B10, and it is a decision rather than a defect.** RemoteViews
         resolves this directory against the SYSTEM uiMode, so a reader running
         Flash in Dark on a Light OS gets the light tile. That is correct: the
         tile lives on the launcher and should match the launcher. It is also
         why someone in Newspaper mode does not get newsprint on their
         wallpaper. Do not add app-theme plumbing to the widget to "fix" this. -->
    <color name="widget_unread_bg">#161D1C</color>
    <color name="widget_unread_text">#E7EBEA</color>
</resources>
